# Security-analysis generated matrices are reproducible; keep committed copies
# (thesis artifacts). Transient node_modules etc. already ignored above.
# Sepolia validation output is environment-specific (generated per run);
# the real public-testnet witness is committed deliberately, not the local dry-run.
4_comparison-framework/results/sepolia_validation.json

# Benchmark harness: only the promoted latest run is tracked
1_blockchain-identity/results/metrics/runs/

# cv2x-testbed Hardhat output (REVIEW_02 Q-9). Only artifacts/contracts/** is
# tracked: the Python providers, tests/conftest.py and
# experiment_pki_vs_erc1056.py --deploy load those three registry artifacts
# without a compile step. Regenerate them with `npx hardhat compile` in
# cv2x-testbed (solc 0.8.20, optimizer 200, no viaIR, evm paris) whenever
# cv2x-testbed/contracts/*.sol changes. Everything else Hardhat writes there
# (build-info, library artifacts such as @openzeppelin/) is build output.
cv2x-testbed/artifacts/*
!cv2x-testbed/artifacts/contracts/
cv2x-testbed/cache/

# Claude Code agent worktrees (local only)
.claude/worktrees/
